@*
    PLAN-003 lot 22 / D13: the one way a step's status is drawn. A failure is red; a failure the
    pipeline was told to continue past is the same red, outlined, with a tooltip saying it did not
    block. Six places used to build this badge themselves, and one of them showed that case orange.
    R-246: a step skipped by its condition reads "Skipped" with its own icon, never "Cancelled".
    An advisory AI step carries a second, neutral "Advisory" badge whatever its status: its failure
    stays visible but is not the run's problem.
*@
<OmniBadge Tone="@BadgeVariant" Fill="@BadgeFill" Icon="@StatusIcon"
           title="@PipelineRunFormatting.StepStatusTitle(Step, L)" Class="@Class">
    @PipelineRunFormatting.StepStatusText(Step, L)
</OmniBadge>
@if (Step.IsAdvisory)
{
    <OmniBadge Tone="OmniTone.Neutral" Fill="OmniFill.Outline" title="@L["StepAdvisoryHint"].Value" Class="@Class">
        @L["StepAdvisory"]
    </OmniBadge>
}
